<!--
The trimming warnings from inside dependencies that our builds excuse, as recelilious approved on
2026-11-21 (docs/design/repository-checks.md section 7). Each entry excuses one warning code in one
method, as an UnconditionalSuppressMessageAttribute that the trimmer applies from this file. The
trimmed test app and the iOS heads pass the file to the trimmer; any other warning still fails
their build.

The entries are every warning that the trimmer reports for protobuf-net and protobuf-net.Core
3.4.40 when it keeps them whole, as the iOS build does: 125 warnings in 118 methods. The trimmed
test app keeps only the code that our libraries reach and reports 11 of them. They come from
protobuf-net's reflection over types that are known only at run time, which the trimmer cannot
follow, and from annotations that its overrides do not match (IL2046, IL2095). SteamKit2
serializes Steam's messages through its compile-time model instead of protobuf-net's runtime
model, and the device check S2.3.8 runs them in the trimmed, ahead-of-time compiled app (C-0009
section 3, docs/design/steam-service.md section 10).

eng/README.md says how the list is made and checked. It changes only with the version of
protobuf-net, in a reviewed change, and goes once the warnings do.
-->
